    "result_text": "The generated `OwnerMapperImpl` calls `fillSelfLink(owner, ownerDto)`, confirming the hook fires for every `OwnerDto` mapping (GET, list/page, created).\n\n## Summary\n\nI agreed with both findings and restructured so the `/api/owners/{id}` scheme lives in exactly one place:\n\n1. **Removed `getSelfLink()` from `Owner.java`** \u2014 the domain entity no longer knows the web layer's URL routing scheme.\n\n2. **Moved self-link construction into `OwnerMapper`** (the DTO/web mapping layer) via an `@AfterMapping` hook, with a single `OWNER_RESOURCE_PATH = \"/api/owners/\"` constant and a `selfLink(id)` helper. Because the collection and page mappings delegate to `toOwnerDto`, the hook populates `selfLink` consistently for GET, list, and created responses \u2014 same observable behaviour as before. The helper guards a null id (returning null) rather than emitting `/api/owners/null`.\n\n3. **Updated `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** to set the 201 `Location` header from `dto.getSelfLink()` instead of rebuilding `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()`. The self link and Location header are the same URL by definition, so they now share one source of truth and can't drift.\n\nThe `openapi.yml` `selfLink` schema property is unchanged (it's what gives `OwnerDto` its getter/setter). Full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
