    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe mechanism is fine \u2014 `getSelfLink()` is a `@Transient` derived getter that MapStruct maps onto `OwnerDto` by name, exactly like the existing `getDisplayName()` and `getInitials()`, so a reader of the DTO mapping will find the field populated consistently for every owner representation (GET, list, created). That part is idiomatic for this codebase.\n\nThe structural problem is *where* the path logic lives and that it is now duplicated:\n\n- **Duplicated literal across two layers.** `Owner.getSelfLink()` builds `\"/api/owners/\" + this.getId()` (src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java:292), and `RespondWithOwnerCreated.service(...)` already builds the identical `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()` for the 201 `Location` header (src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/RespondWithOwnerCreated.java:17). The self-link and the Location header are the same URL by definition, but they're now constructed independently with no shared source of truth \u2014 change the base path and one silently drifts from the other.\n\n- **Layering / catch-all growth on the entity.** The other derived getters on `Owner` (`getDisplayName`, `getInitials`, `getFiscalYear`, etc.) are all intrinsic to owner *data* \u2014 name/date formatting. `getSelfLink()` is different in kind: it hardcodes the web layer's URL routing scheme (`/api/owners/`) into the persistence/domain entity. A maintainer changing the API's base path would not expect to edit the domain model, and the entity shouldn't need to know how it's addressed over HTTP. This is the domain model quietly accreting transport concerns.\n\nSuggested direction (pick one, but unify the two call sites):\n- Extract the `/api/owners/` base path to a single shared constant in the REST layer and have both `RespondWithOwnerCreated` and the self-link construction reference it; or\n- Build the self link in the REST/DTO mapping layer (where the identical Location-header construction already lives) rather than on the domain entity, so the URL scheme stays in one layer and isn't repeated.\n\nEither way the goal is: one place that knows the string `/api/owners/{id}`, consumed by both the self-link field and the Location header.",
